WEBVTT

1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:46,125
[gentle music playing]

2
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:57,750
[Ry] <i>My body has become my enemy.</i>

3
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:03,125
<i>But here I am,</i>
<i>just another particle of the Earth.</i>

4
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:07,000
<i>The ocean doesn't care about sickness</i>

5
00:01:07,083 --> 00:01:09,875
<i>or life and death.</i>

6
00:01:09,958 --> 00:01:12,791
<i>It doesn't care for</i>
<i>our struggles or our pain.</i>

7
00:01:14,458 --> 00:01:17,375
<i>Or that I would have given everything…</i>

8
00:01:18,666 --> 00:01:20,791
<i>…for one last summer like this.</i>

9
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:24,333
<i>One last sunrise…</i>

10
00:01:25,625 --> 00:01:27,041
<i>…with him.</i>

11
00:01:30,166 --> 00:01:32,125
{\an8}[♪ Kye Kye sings "People"]

12
00:01:36,458 --> 00:01:39,000
♪ ♪

13
00:02:01,791 --> 00:02:04,333
♪ <i>I still yearn to be</i> ♪

14
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:07,000
♪ <i>love without a need to please</i> ♪

15
00:02:07,083 --> 00:02:08,916
♪ <i>Help me, help me</i> ♪

16
00:02:11,666 --> 00:02:15,208
{\an8}♪ <i>Silent crave to have childish peace</i> ♪

17
00:02:15,291 --> 00:02:17,000
♪ <i>while weary things</i> ♪

18
00:02:17,083 --> 00:02:18,958
-[ears ringing, heart beating]
-♪ <i>haunt me, haunt me</i> ♪

19
00:02:19,041 --> 00:02:21,375
-♪ <i>Like falling in my sleep…</i>
-[breathes shakily]

20
00:02:21,458 --> 00:02:23,458
[music continues low and distorted]

21
00:02:23,541 --> 00:02:26,083
[shallow gasping]

22
00:02:27,166 --> 00:02:29,375
Ry. Ry.

23
00:02:29,458 --> 00:02:31,333
-[shallow gasping continues]
-[heart beating faster]

24
00:02:31,416 --> 00:02:34,125
[tense music playing]

25
00:02:34,208 --> 00:02:36,250
Ry!

26
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:37,541
Move, move, move!

27
00:02:37,625 --> 00:02:39,083
I got her. Okay.

28
00:02:39,166 --> 00:02:40,208
Okay, breathe.

29
00:02:40,291 --> 00:02:42,583
Breathe, Ry.
You got to breathe, sweetheart.

30
00:02:46,041 --> 00:02:49,291
At this stage, Oriah,
I would strongly recommend surgery.

31
00:02:49,375 --> 00:02:51,708
{\an8}There's still a chance
we can remove all the tubers,

32
00:02:51,791 --> 00:02:54,250
{\an8}and you could be seizure-free.

33
00:02:54,333 --> 00:02:57,166
{\an8}And there's an equal chance
that I'll lose my memory.

34
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:02,666
{\an8}People, places, how to walk,
how to dance, how to live.

35
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:05,291
Everything that makes me a person.

36
00:03:05,375 --> 00:03:07,125
Ry, this is your life we're talking about.

37
00:03:07,208 --> 00:03:09,875
Exactly, Mom. It's my life.

38
00:03:09,958 --> 00:03:12,041
{\an8}Okay, we could increase the medication,

39
00:03:12,125 --> 00:03:14,708
{\an8}but it'll most likely increase
the side effects.

40
00:03:14,791 --> 00:03:16,750
{\an8}I would set alarms
so you don't miss a dose,

41
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:19,083
{\an8}or they won't work properly.

42
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:21,083
{\an8}Can you commit to that?

43
00:03:22,750 --> 00:03:25,333
Ry. Ry.

44
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,875
Honey, I know they make you
feel like shit.

45
00:03:30,958 --> 00:03:32,541
{\an8}Correction.

46
00:03:32,625 --> 00:03:34,708
{\an8}They don't let me feel anything.

47
00:03:34,791 --> 00:03:36,833
All right, Lena, be sure to book a driver
to take her

48
00:03:36,916 --> 00:03:38,583
-wherever she wants to go.
-Yeah.

49
00:03:38,666 --> 00:03:41,416
Also, there's a pharmacy
two streets over from the hotel

50
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,375
where you can fill her prescription.

51
00:03:43,458 --> 00:03:45,083
Other than that,
it's just the usual things

52
00:03:45,166 --> 00:03:46,583
{\an8}we need to be mindful of
with her epilepsy:

53
00:03:46,666 --> 00:03:48,875
{\an8}flashing lights, get good sleep,

54
00:03:48,958 --> 00:03:50,875
no stress, no alcohol.

55
00:03:50,958 --> 00:03:53,541
Great. The nuns and I will be having
our hot girl summer.

56
00:03:54,708 --> 00:03:57,000
So, days one through four are super busy

57
00:03:57,083 --> 00:03:59,416
with the location manager
and Redwyn attorneys.

58
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:01,791
I'll try to schedule some time off, but--

59
00:04:01,875 --> 00:04:03,333
What about spending time together?

60
00:04:05,541 --> 00:04:07,166
Mom, you promised to show me
where you grew up.

61
00:04:07,250 --> 00:04:10,916
No, honey, we are gonna spend
lots of time together.

62
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,375
We have six whole weeks.

63
00:04:12,458 --> 00:04:14,458
We're gonna have fun. It's Mallorca.

64
00:04:14,541 --> 00:04:16,583
As long as you keep your promise.

65
00:04:28,458 --> 00:04:30,583
Thank you.

66
00:04:30,666 --> 00:04:32,291
All right, let me see that schedule again.

67
00:04:32,375 --> 00:04:33,583
[Lena] Yes.

68
00:04:33,666 --> 00:04:36,000
{\an8}[♪ Sofia Kourtesis sings "Madres"]

69
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,458
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

70
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:53,708
[tires screech]

71
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:56,708
♪ ♪

72
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:15,291
<i>Hola.</i>

73
00:05:15,375 --> 00:05:16,833
[hotel manager] Welcome.

74
00:05:18,166 --> 00:05:20,083
We're expecting you, Miss Pera.

75
00:05:20,166 --> 00:05:22,291
-Oh, call me Isolde. Hi.
-Welcome.

76
00:05:22,375 --> 00:05:24,625
<i>Muchas gracias. </i>Thank you.

77
00:05:24,708 --> 00:05:27,500
This is my daughter Oriah. Honey.

78
00:05:27,583 --> 00:05:28,791
-Hi.
-She's a bit jet-lagged.

79
00:05:28,875 --> 00:05:30,458
-Hi.
-Why don't you get settled,

80
00:05:30,541 --> 00:05:32,166
and I'll meet you in the room, okay?

81
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:33,708
I have a quick conference call.

82
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:35,541
[hotel manager] Our concierge team
is looking forward

83
00:05:35,625 --> 00:05:36,791
<i>-to meeting you.</i>
-[indistinct chatter]

84
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:40,875
[Amara German accent] Hi there,

85
00:05:40,958 --> 00:05:42,208
and welcome to our hotel.

86
00:05:42,291 --> 00:05:44,458
-Hi.
-How was your flight?

87
00:05:44,541 --> 00:05:46,166
-It was fine.
-Good.

88
00:05:46,250 --> 00:05:48,583
Oh, sorry, you have a little something.

89
00:05:48,666 --> 00:05:50,166
Ah! [chuckles]

90
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:53,041
I saw it on TikTok.
This took me 20 minutes.

91
00:05:53,125 --> 00:05:54,875
Tell me, honestly,

92
00:05:54,958 --> 00:05:57,583
is it worth investing the time
on the other eye?

93
00:05:58,625 --> 00:06:01,416
Given it's company time,
I'd say yes. [chuckles]

94
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:03,541
Mm. I like you.

95
00:06:03,625 --> 00:06:05,041
Follow me. Right,
I'll show you to your room.

96
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:06,208
This way.

97
00:06:06,291 --> 00:06:08,125
-[Amara] I'm Amara, by the way.
-[Ry] I'm Ry.

98
00:06:08,208 --> 00:06:10,333
[Amara] Okay, so this is the lobby.

99
00:06:10,416 --> 00:06:11,791
You can come find me here
anytime you need.

100
00:06:11,875 --> 00:06:15,208
So, what brings you
to our Spanish paradise?

101
00:06:15,291 --> 00:06:17,958
-My mom's closing a real estate deal.
-Uh-huh?

102
00:06:18,041 --> 00:06:19,958
Yeah, her company wants
to build a new hotel.

103
00:06:20,041 --> 00:06:22,583
[gasps] Ooh, another hotel. How exciting.

104
00:06:22,666 --> 00:06:24,500
The locals are gonna love that.

105
00:06:24,583 --> 00:06:25,916
Do you know the island at all?

106
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,166
No. No, it's my first time.

107
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:30,041
I haven't really been out of Texas much.

108
00:06:30,125 --> 00:06:33,083
Wow, a Texan. How exotic.

109
00:06:33,166 --> 00:06:36,750
So, Ry, what do you like to do for fun?

110
00:06:36,833 --> 00:06:37,958
Oh, I don't know.

111
00:06:38,041 --> 00:06:40,416
Maybe go to the beach or lie by the pool.

112
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,875
You can definitely do that,
but there's tons of other stuff.

113
00:06:43,958 --> 00:06:45,875
-Do you like caves?
-Caves?

114
00:06:45,958 --> 00:06:47,125
[Amara] <i>Are you single?</i>

115
00:06:47,208 --> 00:06:49,833
-Yeah.
-Ugh, the locals here are superhot.

116
00:06:49,916 --> 00:06:52,916
They're like this crazy mix
of Carthaginians, then Romans,

117
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,083
then the Catalan settlers
from France and Spain.

118
00:06:55,166 --> 00:06:58,583
Whatever you are into,
it's like a hookup buffet.

119
00:06:58,666 --> 00:07:01,500
Oh, and don't be surprised
if you see goats in trees.

120
00:07:01,583 --> 00:07:03,708
-Goats in trees?
-Yes, goats in trees.

121
00:07:03,791 --> 00:07:04,916
Anyway, the point is,

122
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,500
you're going to have a summer
worth remembering.

123
00:07:07,583 --> 00:07:09,458
Okay, your mother's room
is just across the hall,

124
00:07:09,541 --> 00:07:11,541
and this one's you.

125
00:07:12,916 --> 00:07:14,916
[gentle music playing]

126
00:07:17,958 --> 00:07:20,625
Your mother's company built
an amazing place.

127
00:07:22,083 --> 00:07:23,333
Yeah.

128
00:07:25,458 --> 00:07:27,708
[phone alarm beeping and vibrating]

129
00:07:27,791 --> 00:07:29,541
Sorry.

130
00:07:29,625 --> 00:07:31,541
-[alarm stops]
-I'll let you settle in.

131
00:07:31,625 --> 00:07:33,875
Just give us a call downstairs
if you need anything at all.

132
00:07:33,958 --> 00:07:35,291
<i>Auf Wiedersehen.</i> Bye-bye.

133
00:07:35,375 --> 00:07:37,750
-Thank you, Amara.
-[door closes]

134
00:07:47,666 --> 00:07:49,208
[pills rattle]

135
00:07:57,125 --> 00:07:58,291
[bottle closes]

136
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:01,833
-[waves rolling]
-[seagulls calling]

137
00:08:01,916 --> 00:08:03,833
[Ry] So, what's the plan for tomorrow?

138
00:08:03,916 --> 00:08:05,125
[Isolde] I'm packed.

139
00:08:05,208 --> 00:08:08,291
I have back-to-back meetings
and party planning.

140
00:08:09,166 --> 00:08:10,250
What party?

141
00:08:10,333 --> 00:08:12,291
A fundraiser.

142
00:08:12,375 --> 00:08:15,250
Yeah. In addition to getting them
to let us build the hotel,

143
00:08:15,333 --> 00:08:17,500
in good faith,
we are building an arts center

144
00:08:17,583 --> 00:08:20,041
-for the children of Mallorca.
-That's nice.

145
00:08:20,125 --> 00:08:21,291
[phone chimes]

146
00:08:24,041 --> 00:08:25,583
Everything okay?

147
00:08:25,666 --> 00:08:27,916
Just the-the company. [sighs]

148
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,166
They're checking in
to see if I'll return this fall.

149
00:08:31,208 --> 00:08:32,791
But you are going back, right?

150
00:08:32,875 --> 00:08:34,958
You just need to rest this summer.

151
00:08:35,041 --> 00:08:36,833
And then you're gonna be
back in the saddle.

152
00:08:38,541 --> 00:08:40,208
Yeah.

153
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,458
[Chloe over phone] <i>We're all going out</i>
<i>tonight to celebrate</i>

154
00:08:43,541 --> 00:08:44,750
<i>the end of the season.</i>

155
00:08:44,833 --> 00:08:46,208
<i>We wish you were here.</i>

156
00:08:46,291 --> 00:08:47,583
<i>How are you feeling?</i>

157
00:08:47,666 --> 00:08:49,125
<i>Is the new medication helping?</i>

158
00:08:49,208 --> 00:08:51,958
Uh, it's… [chuckles]
it's an adjustment for sure.

159
00:08:52,041 --> 00:08:54,666
<i>We've all been so worried about you.</i>

160
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:57,416
First of all, don't do that.

161
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:59,250
Second, I am fine.

162
00:08:59,333 --> 00:09:02,791
My mom has this whole thing
planned for tomorrow.

163
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:05,000
She's gonna show me where she grew up.

164
00:09:05,083 --> 00:09:06,541
<i>Your mom is such a queen.</i>

165
00:09:06,625 --> 00:09:07,625
<i>And forget what I said.</i>

166
00:09:07,708 --> 00:09:09,750
<i>I wish we were all there with you guys.</i>

167
00:09:09,833 --> 00:09:10,791
Mm-hmm.

168
00:09:10,875 --> 00:09:12,250
<i>Well, tell me</i>
<i>if you see any hot Spaniards.</i>

169
00:09:12,333 --> 00:09:14,000
<i>-Okay?</i>
-Yeah. For sure.

170
00:09:14,083 --> 00:09:15,750
<i>-We love you, babes. Call me!</i>
-[chuckles]

171
00:09:15,833 --> 00:09:17,750
-[women] <i>See you, Ry!</i>
<i>-Love you.</i>

172
00:09:17,833 --> 00:09:19,833
-Love you. Bye.
-[women] <i>Bye.</i>

173
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:25,333
[phone alarm beeping and vibrating]

174
00:09:25,416 --> 00:09:27,125
-[sighs]
-[alarm stops]

175
00:09:27,208 --> 00:09:29,208
[gentle guitar music playing]

176
00:09:30,291 --> 00:09:31,708
[sputters lips]

177
00:09:43,041 --> 00:09:45,000
♪ ♪

178
00:09:49,375 --> 00:09:51,333
[splashing and laughter in distance]

179
00:09:53,083 --> 00:09:56,125
[splashing and laughter continue]

180
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
[guard] Hey! [shouts in Spanish]

181
00:10:02,375 --> 00:10:04,333
[urgent Spanish chatter]

182
00:10:10,666 --> 00:10:13,500
[birds chirping]

183
00:10:13,583 --> 00:10:16,583
[Isolde] Okay, so we have
around 150 guests.

184
00:10:16,666 --> 00:10:17,833
Ooh, this is pretty.

185
00:10:17,916 --> 00:10:22,500
Hey, Ry, do you like eggshell or oatmeal?

186
00:10:22,583 --> 00:10:24,458
Why do they all have to be
named after food?

187
00:10:24,541 --> 00:10:26,375
[Isolde] I don't know.

188
00:10:27,416 --> 00:10:29,333
[sighs] Honey, why don't you go
do something fun,

189
00:10:29,416 --> 00:10:31,416
and I'll meet up with you later.

190
00:10:32,416 --> 00:10:34,166
-I was gonna hit the beach.
-Well, that's a good idea.

191
00:10:34,250 --> 00:10:36,333
Take the driver. Oh!

192
00:10:36,416 --> 00:10:38,666
And extra meds. And water.

193
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:40,166
And put some sunblock, sweetheart.

194
00:10:40,250 --> 00:10:42,833
-Oh, and, Ry--
-Be careful?

195
00:10:42,916 --> 00:10:44,875
Have fun.

196
00:10:46,791 --> 00:10:48,208
Coconut cream for the win.

197
00:10:48,291 --> 00:10:49,916
[footsteps departing]

198
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,208
See? Pretends not to care, but she does.

199
00:10:52,291 --> 00:10:53,666
Hmm.

200
00:10:57,250 --> 00:10:59,916
-Hi.
-Hi.

201
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,500
Slow morning, was it?

202
00:11:01,583 --> 00:11:03,333
Why?

203
00:11:03,416 --> 00:11:04,416
[chuckles] Your eyes.

204
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,041
-Oh.
-I love the eyeliner.

205
00:11:06,125 --> 00:11:07,166
-Thank you.
-[chuckles]

206
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:08,833
So, where to?

207
00:11:08,916 --> 00:11:12,791
Oh, actually, yes, I was gonna ask you
if you had any beach recommendations.

208
00:11:12,875 --> 00:11:15,416
I think I know just the spot.

209
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,708
-It's a real hidden gem.
-Ooh.

210
00:11:17,791 --> 00:11:19,125
-Thank you.
-Enjoy.

211
00:11:20,166 --> 00:11:21,833
Perfect.

212
00:11:21,916 --> 00:11:24,500
[♪ Bad Bunny and The Marias
sing "Otro Atardecer"]

213
00:11:34,833 --> 00:11:36,791
♪ ♪

214
00:11:43,125 --> 00:11:45,083
[quiet chatter]

215
00:11:54,375 --> 00:11:56,375
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

216
00:12:18,166 --> 00:12:20,125
♪ ♪

217
00:12:47,458 --> 00:12:49,416
♪ ♪

218
00:12:58,416 --> 00:13:00,416
[song fades]

219
00:13:05,250 --> 00:13:07,208
[quiet chatter]

220
00:13:33,333 --> 00:13:35,333
[laughter in distance]

221
00:13:39,083 --> 00:13:41,083
[laughter continues]

222
00:13:45,958 --> 00:13:47,125
[sighs heavily]

223
00:13:47,208 --> 00:13:50,000
["Otro Atardecer" resumes
with lyrics in Spanish]

224
00:14:03,166 --> 00:14:04,583
[laughs]

225
00:14:06,291 --> 00:14:09,000
-[song fades]
-[laughter, quiet chatter]

226
00:14:10,041 --> 00:14:12,041
[gentle music playing]

227
00:14:36,708 --> 00:14:38,958
♪ ♪

228
00:14:51,166 --> 00:14:53,166
[music fades]

229
00:14:55,666 --> 00:14:57,666
Can I help you?

230
00:14:58,875 --> 00:15:02,416
Uh… um, no, no.

231
00:15:03,416 --> 00:15:04,625
It's rude to stare, <i>señorita.</i>

232
00:15:04,708 --> 00:15:06,250
I wasn't… I wasn't staring.

233
00:15:06,333 --> 00:15:08,166
I was just, uh, uh…

234
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:10,166
I was looking behind you.

235
00:15:11,791 --> 00:15:14,166
[Julian] Wow. Nice view.

236
00:15:16,416 --> 00:15:18,291
[chuckles nervously]
Okay, well, I'm gonna go.

237
00:15:18,375 --> 00:15:20,541
-Yeah, you should go.
-Excuse me?

238
00:15:20,625 --> 00:15:22,916
I said that you should go.

239
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,416
Did I do something?
Uh, do you have a problem?

240
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:27,166
I do have a problem.

241
00:15:27,250 --> 00:15:29,583
This is a locals' beach.

242
00:15:29,666 --> 00:15:32,875
We prefer when tourists don't
stare at us while we sunbathe.

243
00:15:32,958 --> 00:15:34,083
Uh, I'm so sorry.

244
00:15:34,166 --> 00:15:35,250
I hadn't realized
it was a locals-only beach.

245
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:36,375
I just wanted to swim.

246
00:15:36,458 --> 00:15:38,291
Well, I think you might find the pool

247
00:15:38,375 --> 00:15:41,291
at the Marès & Mar Hotel more comfortable.

248
00:15:41,375 --> 00:15:42,416
How'd you--

