she had nothing.

1016
00:54:30,875 --> 00:54:34,041
But she worked her ass off, and…

1017
00:54:37,291 --> 00:54:39,125
…what she's accomplished
is pretty amazing.

1018
00:54:40,916 --> 00:54:42,375
She's had a lot of success and…

1019
00:54:43,416 --> 00:54:45,125
-[chuckles]
-What?

1020
00:54:45,208 --> 00:54:47,458
I'm so sorry, but…

1021
00:54:47,541 --> 00:54:48,875
it just surprise me sometimes

1022
00:54:48,958 --> 00:54:51,916
what Americans define as success.

1023
00:54:52,000 --> 00:54:53,666
What do you mean?

1024
00:54:55,000 --> 00:54:58,916
I mean, it seems like
you just work and work

1025
00:54:59,000 --> 00:55:00,958
-[chuckles]
-just to go on vacation

1026
00:55:01,041 --> 00:55:03,583
and then buy more and more and…

1027
00:55:05,000 --> 00:55:06,833
I don't know. Look at our lives here.

1028
00:55:06,916 --> 00:55:07,875
Mm-hmm.

1029
00:55:07,958 --> 00:55:09,041
Sure, we have problems,

1030
00:55:09,125 --> 00:55:12,916
but we are more than happy
with what we have.

1031
00:55:13,000 --> 00:55:14,250
What else could we want?

1032
00:55:14,333 --> 00:55:17,041
Even Miss America ended up on my boat.

1033
00:55:18,500 --> 00:55:23,125
Sometimes you just
have to enjoy what you have

1034
00:55:23,208 --> 00:55:24,958
while you have it.

1035
00:55:26,750 --> 00:55:28,291
Does that make sense?

1036
00:55:31,416 --> 00:55:33,250
More than you know.

1037
00:55:35,708 --> 00:55:37,750
Being here…

1038
00:55:39,708 --> 00:55:42,791
…this place, this summer, it's…

1039
00:55:42,875 --> 00:55:45,375
really made me think about
where I want to be.

1040
00:55:49,083 --> 00:55:51,000
Well…

1041
00:55:51,083 --> 00:55:55,666
there's never been anywhere else on Earth
I want to be than right here.

1042
00:56:08,166 --> 00:56:10,000
[whispers] Can I see your room?

1043
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:14,583
[♪ Love Spells sings "Love Costs"]

1044
00:56:25,541 --> 00:56:27,916
♪ <i>You could never die</i> ♪

1045
00:56:29,041 --> 00:56:32,041
♪ <i>I'll always keep you alive</i> ♪

1046
00:56:33,666 --> 00:56:36,375
♪ <i>Think about you all the time</i> ♪

1047
00:56:37,875 --> 00:56:40,708
♪ <i>My security in life</i> ♪

1048
00:56:42,416 --> 00:56:44,916
♪ <i>And when I'm low</i> ♪

1049
00:56:46,291 --> 00:56:49,416
♪ <i>you get me high like coke</i> ♪

1050
00:56:50,958 --> 00:56:53,375
♪ <i>How could I let you go?</i> ♪

1051
00:56:55,291 --> 00:56:56,708
♪ <i>I'll never know</i> ♪

1052
00:56:57,750 --> 00:57:02,416
♪ <i>You could play me like a song</i> ♪

1053
00:57:02,500 --> 00:57:06,375
♪ <i>and I'll still sing along</i> ♪

1054
00:57:06,458 --> 00:57:10,000
♪ <i>The only tune I know…</i>

1055
00:57:10,083 --> 00:57:11,458
[breathing heavily]

1056
00:57:11,541 --> 00:57:14,916
♪ <i>Love you till we're bones</i> ♪

1057
00:57:16,708 --> 00:57:20,875
♪ <i>What else can I say?</i> ♪

1058
00:57:20,958 --> 00:57:25,166
♪ <i>Another time maybe</i> ♪

1059
00:57:25,250 --> 00:57:28,250
♪ <i>And I don't got the heart</i> ♪

1060
00:57:28,333 --> 00:57:32,041
♪ <i>to leave you in this way</i> ♪

1061
00:57:33,791 --> 00:57:38,083
♪ <i>Another heartbreak</i> ♪

1062
00:57:38,166 --> 00:57:42,333
♪ <i>The cycle breaks me</i> ♪

1063
00:57:42,416 --> 00:57:45,375
♪ <i>I have myself to blame</i> ♪

1064
00:57:45,458 --> 00:57:49,375
♪ <i>for hurting in this way</i> ♪

1065
00:57:49,458 --> 00:57:53,875
♪ <i>You could play me like a song</i> ♪

1066
00:57:53,958 --> 00:57:58,333
-♪ <i>and I'll still sing along</i> ♪
-[breathing heavily, moaning]

1067
00:57:58,416 --> 00:58:01,833
♪ <i>Hold you till we're bones</i> ♪

1068
00:58:02,833 --> 00:58:06,625
♪ <i>Hold you till we're bones</i> ♪

1069
00:58:11,083 --> 00:58:14,916
♪ <i>Hold you till we're bones</i> ♪

1070
00:58:19,875 --> 00:58:22,291
♪ <i>Hold you till we're bones</i> ♪♪

1071
00:58:22,375 --> 00:58:23,583
[song fades]

1072
00:58:27,583 --> 00:58:29,500
[Lena] Okay, um, do you mind having--

1073
00:58:29,583 --> 00:58:31,416
Oh. Hi.

1074
00:58:31,500 --> 00:58:33,208
-How are you feeling?
-Great.

1075
00:58:33,291 --> 00:58:35,208
You look radiant and happy.

1076
00:58:35,291 --> 00:58:37,541
I am.

1077
00:58:40,375 --> 00:58:41,875
Okay, I don't want to know.

1078
00:58:41,958 --> 00:58:43,291
As long as you're being safe.

1079
00:58:43,375 --> 00:58:44,708
You don't know
these Spanish boys like I do.

1080
00:58:44,791 --> 00:58:45,916
Had I stayed on this island,

1081
00:58:46,000 --> 00:58:48,083
Lord knows how many brothers
and sisters you'd have.

1082
00:58:48,166 --> 00:58:50,250
[laughs] Mom, please.

1083
00:58:50,333 --> 00:58:51,583
Uh, if you have a second,

1084
00:58:51,666 --> 00:58:53,833
I would love to talk to you
about the dance company.

1085
00:58:53,916 --> 00:58:55,791
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-[Lena] Sorry.

1086
00:58:55,875 --> 00:58:57,500
[Isolde] Oh, no,
I don't like it. That one.

1087
00:58:57,583 --> 00:58:59,000
-That one.
-Okay, okay, we'll change it.

1088
00:58:59,083 --> 00:59:01,041
Wait. Do you know the Garcias?

1089
00:59:01,125 --> 00:59:02,916
Yeah. That's the company we're buying.

1090
00:59:04,833 --> 00:59:06,791
I thought you had all the land you needed.

1091
00:59:06,875 --> 00:59:08,750
Yeah, the Garcias own
some of the most valuable docks

1092
00:59:08,833 --> 00:59:10,791
-on the island.
-And we can't build the hotel

1093
00:59:10,875 --> 00:59:12,458
unless we buy them.

1094
00:59:17,166 --> 00:59:19,000
That's the boy you're seeing?

1095
00:59:19,083 --> 00:59:20,916
A Garcia?

1096
00:59:24,250 --> 00:59:26,958
-Lena, can I get the room?
-Of course.

1097
00:59:27,041 --> 00:59:29,791
Excuse me. Would you just mind
following me and showing me…

1098
00:59:29,875 --> 00:59:31,708
-Honey, I--
-No, Mom, please don't do this.

1099
00:59:31,791 --> 00:59:33,250
I know the situation. Don't--

1100
00:59:33,333 --> 00:59:34,708
Honey, this is for the best, okay?

1101
00:59:34,791 --> 00:59:36,291
Their business is…

1102
00:59:36,375 --> 00:59:37,583
-it's over.
-No, it's not.

1103
00:59:37,666 --> 00:59:39,458
They're just waiting for a loan.
They need more time.

1104
00:59:39,541 --> 00:59:42,041
Another loan?

1105
00:59:42,125 --> 00:59:44,416
That is just gonna put them
further into debt.

1106
00:59:46,583 --> 00:59:48,541
I'm giving them independence. Okay?

1107
00:59:48,625 --> 00:59:51,166
Freedom from being trapped
inside a failing business.

1108
00:59:51,250 --> 00:59:52,750
But they're not trapped though.

1109
00:59:52,833 --> 00:59:55,541
They love it here. They love what they do.

1110
00:59:56,666 --> 01:00:00,291
To them, it's just…
it's not about money.

1111
01:00:00,375 --> 01:00:02,083
It's so much more than that.

1112
01:00:02,166 --> 01:00:03,875
It's family, and it's where they're from.

1113
01:00:03,958 --> 01:00:07,291
No, I know. I know the Garcias.

1114
01:00:07,375 --> 01:00:09,875
And I feel for them.

1115
01:00:09,958 --> 01:00:11,750
Okay? I do.

1116
01:00:11,833 --> 01:00:12,958
But between you and I,

1117
01:00:13,041 --> 01:00:15,500
I offered them double
than what it's worth.

1118
01:00:15,583 --> 01:00:16,666
I'm not the villain here.

1119
01:00:16,750 --> 01:00:19,375
Mateo Garcia is never gonna have to work
another day in his life, nor his son.

1120
01:00:19,458 --> 01:00:20,833
It's not about that.

1121
01:00:20,916 --> 01:00:22,791
This is what makes them happy.

1122
01:00:22,875 --> 01:00:25,375
Mom, this gives them purpose.

1123
01:00:28,375 --> 01:00:31,666
[chuckles] You know,
it's easy to be idealistic, okay?

1124
01:00:31,750 --> 01:00:34,166
But business is business.
It's-it's not personal.

1125
01:00:36,166 --> 01:00:38,000
Please.

1126
01:00:39,958 --> 01:00:41,416
Please.

1127
01:00:43,208 --> 01:00:44,916
For me.

1128
01:00:46,833 --> 01:00:50,250
Okay, look, I'll see what I can do,
but I'm not promising anything, okay?

1129
01:00:54,125 --> 01:00:59,083
-[♪ Esha Tewari sings "In Twos"]
-♪ <i>I'll catch the train again</i> ♪

1130
01:00:59,166 --> 01:01:03,708
♪ <i>Starry-eyed</i>
<i>and I'm stalking your mind…</i>

1131
01:01:03,791 --> 01:01:05,583
Can I talk to you about something?

1132
01:01:07,875 --> 01:01:12,458
♪ <i>The light that you lead home</i> ♪

1133
01:01:12,541 --> 01:01:13,625
♪ <i>Drink a jug…</i>

1134
01:01:13,708 --> 01:01:18,416
Can we just have one day
where we forget it all?

1135
01:01:18,500 --> 01:01:19,625
Please?

1136
01:01:21,625 --> 01:01:22,791
-Yeah.
-[song ends]

1137
01:01:22,875 --> 01:01:25,166
[uplifting music playing]

1138
01:01:52,625 --> 01:01:54,583
♪ ♪

1139
01:01:59,375 --> 01:02:01,375
-[Isolde] Ry, sweetie?
-[knock on door]

1140
01:02:01,458 --> 01:02:03,083
Are you here? Hey.

1141
01:02:03,166 --> 01:02:07,416
I have meetings all day,
but I wanted to see you before I left.

1142
01:02:07,500 --> 01:02:09,416
Did you refill your meds? Oh.

1143
01:02:09,500 --> 01:02:12,833
I got you two dresses,
this green and pink,

1144
01:02:12,916 --> 01:02:15,291
so let me know which one
you want to wear to the fundraiser.

1145
01:02:15,375 --> 01:02:18,125
Did you figure something out
for the Garcias?

1146
01:02:18,208 --> 01:02:21,541
Not yet, but I am working on it, okay?

1147
01:02:21,625 --> 01:02:22,791
[knock on door]

1148
01:02:22,875 --> 01:02:24,375
[Lena] Sorry, we're running late.

1149
01:02:24,458 --> 01:02:25,416
Yeah, here.

1150
01:02:25,500 --> 01:02:28,083
I'm gonna be busy today,
but why don't we have breakfast tomorrow.

1151
01:02:29,416 --> 01:02:31,458
You feeling okay?

1152
01:02:31,541 --> 01:02:33,583
You look a little pale.

1153
01:02:33,666 --> 01:02:35,125
I'm good.

1154
01:02:36,166 --> 01:02:38,208
Okay. I love you.

1155
01:02:38,291 --> 01:02:40,041
See you later.

1156
01:02:40,125 --> 01:02:42,125
[door opens, closes]

1157
01:02:43,166 --> 01:02:44,541
[phone chimes and vibrates]

1158
01:02:51,250 --> 01:02:53,208
[gentle music playing]

1159
01:02:54,666 --> 01:02:56,208
[Julian] <i>Do you trust me?</i>

1160
01:02:57,291 --> 01:02:58,541
Yeah.

1161
01:03:00,541 --> 01:03:02,416
Turn off the light.

1162
01:03:05,208 --> 01:03:06,250
Okay.

1163
01:03:15,958 --> 01:03:19,833
This… is my favorite feeling.

1164
01:03:21,125 --> 01:03:24,250
You just melt into everything around you.

1165
01:03:25,291 --> 01:03:28,375
It helps me forget about the problems
when the lights are on.

1166
01:03:31,791 --> 01:03:34,791
It's good to face your fears, Oriah.

1167
01:03:37,333 --> 01:03:39,833
How else can you overcome them?

1168
01:03:39,916 --> 01:03:41,916
♪ ♪

1169
01:03:50,166 --> 01:03:52,375
[♪ Levitation Room sings "Pienso en Ti"]

1170
01:03:52,458 --> 01:03:54,458
[seagulls squawking]

1171
01:04:00,166 --> 01:04:02,708
This is where we met. [chuckles]

1172
01:04:05,083 --> 01:04:06,291
Wait here.

1173
01:04:06,375 --> 01:04:08,375
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

1174
01:04:21,000 --> 01:04:23,166
If you can't swim, I can help you.

1175
01:04:23,250 --> 01:04:24,541
[Julian chuckles]

1176
01:04:32,083 --> 01:04:34,083
♪ ♪

1177
01:04:50,541 --> 01:04:52,458
-[song fades]
-[phone ringing and vibrating]

1178
01:04:52,541 --> 01:04:54,583
[chuckles]

1179
01:04:54,666 --> 01:04:56,041
Hey.

1180
01:04:56,125 --> 01:04:58,125
[Chloe over phone] <i>Why do you look</i>
<i>like you just got laid?</i>

1181
01:04:58,208 --> 01:05:00,541
-[Ry laughs]
<i>-Okay, spill the tea.</i>

1182
01:05:00,625 --> 01:05:02,958
Let's just say we have
a lot of catching up to do.

1183
01:05:03,041 --> 01:05:04,833
<i>What is happening on that island?</i>

1184
01:05:04,916 --> 01:05:06,750
<i>Tell me everything.</i>

1185
01:05:06,833 --> 01:05:08,708
Dude, I think I'm in love.

1186
01:05:09,833 --> 01:05:12,625
[chuckles] Like, on a cellular level.

1187
01:05:12,708 --> 01:05:16,041
<i>On a cell-- Who even are you right now?</i>

1188
01:05:16,125 --> 01:05:17,750
-[laughs]
<i>-Okay, what-what are you gonna do?</i>

1189
01:05:17,833 --> 01:05:20,416
<i>Aren't you coming home</i>
<i>in a couple of days?</i>

1190
01:05:21,500 --> 01:05:22,541
I don't know.

1191
01:05:22,625 --> 01:05:23,958
<i>Wow.</i>

1192
01:05:24,041 --> 01:05:25,791
<i>So this is serious?</i>

1193
01:05:25,875 --> 01:05:27,750
Romeo and Juliet serious.

1194
01:05:27,833 --> 01:05:29,541
<i>Wait, didn't one of them die?</i>

1195
01:05:29,625 --> 01:05:31,375
-[knock on door]
-[Lena] Hey, it's Lena.

1196
01:05:31,458 --> 01:05:33,708
-I have to go.
-[Chloe] <i>Okay, talk soon. Call me.</i>

1197
01:05:33,791 --> 01:05:35,000
Yeah?

1198
01:05:36,375 --> 01:05:38,541
Hi, Ry. Your mom's
not gonna make it this morning.

1199
01:05:38,625 --> 01:05:40,083
-[door closes]
-With the event tonight,

1200
01:05:40,166 --> 01:05:42,583
she's being pulled
in a million directions.

1201
01:05:42,666 --> 01:05:44,958
Look, I know it's not my place to say…

1202
01:05:46,000 --> 01:05:47,500
but…

1203
01:05:47,583 --> 01:05:49,916
the Garcias have agreed to sell.

1204
01:05:51,500 --> 01:05:53,708
They're signing with Redwyn now.

1205
01:05:54,833 --> 01:05:56,625
-What?
-I'm so sorry, Ry.

1206
01:05:56,708 --> 01:05:57,708
I have to go.

1207
01:05:57,791 --> 01:05:59,750
[line ringing]

1208
01:05:59,833 --> 01:06:02,041
[Julian speaking Spanish
in voicemail recording]

1209
01:06:02,125 --> 01:06:03,333
[phone beeps]

1210
01:06:04,416 --> 01:06:06,416
[panting]

1211
01:06:08,458 --> 01:06:09,458
[grunts]

1212
01:06:09,541 --> 01:06:11,541
[tense music playing]

1213
01:06:18,833 --> 01:06:20,708
No.

1214
01:06:20,791 --> 01:06:21,916
[exhales sharply]

1215
01:06:32,375 --> 01:06:33,625
Julian!

1216
01:06:34,708 --> 01:06:36,791
Julian, what happened?

1217
01:06:37,875 --> 01:06:39,708
Who did this?

1218
01:06:39,791 --> 01:06:41,916
It was Carlos.

1219
01:06:42,000 --> 01:06:43,416
Last night.

1220
01:06:45,041 --> 01:06:46,250
Now my father…

1221
01:06:48,625 --> 01:06:50,458
It was the final straw.

1222
01:06:51,458 --> 01:06:53,541
He signed with Redwyn.

1223
01:07:00,375 --> 01:07:01,541
It's all my fault.

1224
01:07:05,000 --> 01:07:06,291
No.

1225
01:07:08,333 --> 01:07:09,500
No, it's not.

1226
01:07:14,625 --> 01:07:16,291
Julian, my mom works for Redwyn.

1227
01:07:22,833 --> 01:07:24,291
I'm so sorry. I just found out--

1228
01:07:24,375 --> 01:07:25,958
You need to leave, Ry.

1229
01:07:26,041 --> 01:07:28,458
-What? But I just--
-Leave!

1230
01:07:28,541 --> 01:07:29,708
Leave.

1231
01:07:37,041 --> 01:07:38,583
[sniffles]

1232
01:07:39,583 --> 01:07:41,208
Mom?

1233
01:07:41,291 --> 01:07:42,625
Mom, what happened?

1234
01:07:42,708 --> 01:07:45,458
Could you give me a moment? Thank you.

1235
01:07:45,541 --> 01:07:47,375
You promised you would help them.

1236
01:07:47,458 --> 01:07:48,791
Honey, I did.

1237
01:07:48,875 --> 01:07:51,166
They had a sinking business,
and I threw them a lifeline.

1238
01:07:51,250 --> 01:07:53,458
[chuckles] Oh, so now
they have money and things

1239
01:07:53,541 --> 01:07:55,250
and no pride and no roots, just like you.

1240
01:07:55,333 --> 01:07:56,541
What does that mean?

1241
01:07:56,625 --> 01:07:58,958
It means you measure everything
with money.

1242
01:07:59,041 --> 01:08:01,958
You love power.
You're this power suit boss.

1243
01:08:02,041 --> 01:08:04,166
[stammers] You brought me
to where you're from,

1244
01:08:04,250 --> 01:08:06,458
and you've barely left the hotel.

1245
01:08:08,541 --> 01:08:10,333
Why do you even do all of this?

1246
01:08:11,916 --> 01:08:13,625
Why?

1247
01:08:13,708 --> 01:08:16,291
Why do I do this? I do this for you.

1248
01:08:18,041 --> 01:08:20,041
How do you not see that?

1249
01:08:20,125 --> 01:08:22,250
You think I like being busy all the time?

1250
01:08:22,333 --> 01:08:25,458
Of course I want to spend time with you.

1251
01:08:25,541 --> 01:08:28,375
But I also thank God every day
that I have this job,

1252
01:08:28,458 --> 01:08:30,541
which I'm really good at,

1253
01:08:30,625 --> 01:08:32,500
because that means
I can take care of you, Ry.

1254
01:08:32,583 --> 01:08:35,250
In every way that you need.

1255
01:08:38,708 --> 01:08:40,125
You're my purpose.

1256
01:08:41,208 --> 01:08:42,375
Okay? So…

1257
01:08:43,916 --> 01:08:45,958
If I could've changed
the outcome for the Garcias,

1258
01:08:46,041 --> 01:08:47,375
I would have.

1259
01:08:48,875 --> 01:08:50,333
Believe me, I would have.

1260
01:08:54,416 --> 01:08:55,500
[sighs]

1261
01:08:55,583 --> 01:08:58,166
So let's… let's just
take a deep breath…

1262
01:08:59,916 --> 01:09:02,458
…and get ready for the gala.

1263
01:09:02,541 --> 01:09:05,166
It is such an important night.

1264
01:09:05,250 --> 01:09:08,500
We only have a few days left here,
and I need you.

1265
01:09:09,791 --> 01:09:11,791
[pensive music playing]

1266
01:09:14,041 --> 01:09:15,541
[sighs]

1267
01:09:21,208 --> 01:09:22,541
[exhales heavily]

1268
01:09:22,625 --> 01:09:24,625
[taking off shoes]

1269
01:09:30,875 --> 01:09:31,875
[sniffles]

1270
01:09:38,083 --> 01:09:39,458
[inhales sharply]

1271
01:09:39,541 --> 01:09:41,333
[sighs]

1272
01:09:48,458 --> 01:09:49,583
[exhales shakily]

1273
01:09:49,666 --> 01:09:51,083
[whimpers]

1274
01:09:55,708 --> 01:09:57,083
[sobbing]

1275
01:10:01,791 --> 01:10:03,208
[sniffles]

1276
01:10:04,916 --> 01:10:06,916
♪ ♪

1277
01:10:23,958 --> 01:10:25,208
Oh.

1278
01:10:26,416 --> 01:10:28,583
I know you were having,
like, a super intense

1279
01:10:28,666 --> 01:10:30,541
mirror stare-off thing with yourself,

1280
01:10:30,625 --> 01:10:34,875
but for the record, you look hot.

1281
01:10:36,333 --> 01:10:39,500
And none of this is your fault,
by the way.

1282
01:10:39,583 --> 01:10:42,625
This is just the way the world works.

1283
01:10:42,708 --> 01:10:45,333
If it wasn't you guys,
it would've just been somebody else.

1284
01:10:45,416 --> 01:10:47,166
-[sighs]
-Hmm?

1285
01:10:47,250 --> 01:10:48,666
[whispers] Probably uglier.

1286
01:10:49,791 --> 01:10:52,708
-[laughs]
-Julian will come around.

1287
01:10:52,791 --> 01:10:54,666
[whispers] I promise.

1288
01:10:54,750 --> 01:10:57,666
[band playing "Tangos de la Juderia"]

1289
01:10:57,750 --> 01:10:59,750
-[lively chatter]
-[music continues]

1290
01:11:07,250 --> 01:11:09,250
[Isolde talking indistinctly under music]

1291
01:11:11,166 --> 01:11:13,083
♪ ♪

1292
01:11:13,166 --> 01:11:15,166
[indistinct chatter continues]

1293
01:11:19,250 --> 01:11:21,250
[insects trilling]

1294
01:11:23,958 --> 01:11:25,541
[sighs]

1295
01:11:35,291 --> 01:11:36,458
No.

1296
01:11:37,791 --> 01:11:39,083
Fucking chemicals.

1297
01:11:39,166 --> 01:11:40,375
[grunts]

1298
01:11:40,458 --> 01:11:42,458
[panting]

1299
01:11:46,125 --> 01:11:47,958
[calling whistle]

1300
01:11:48,041 --> 01:11:50,041
[speaking Catalan]

1301
01:11:53,375 --> 01:11:55,541
What do you want?

1302
01:11:55,625 --> 01:11:57,500
You know…

1303
01:11:57,583 --> 01:11:59,500
your boyfriend… [smacks lips]

1304
01:11:59,583 --> 01:12:00,958
he owes me a lot of money.

1305
01:12:02,166 --> 01:12:04,583
And since you seem so fond
of his beautiful face,

1306
01:12:04,666 --> 01:12:07,541
I thought you'd like to stop me
from ruining it, no?

1307
01:12:08,625 --> 01:12:09,750
You'll get your money.

1308
01:12:09,833 --> 01:12:12,583
Slow down, <i>reina.</i>

1309
01:12:12,666 --> 01:12:15,208
Not everything has to be about cash.

1310
01:12:15,291 --> 01:12:17,666
-Some things are worth more than money.
-[whimpers]

1311
01:12:17,750 --> 01:12:19,875
Like food, wine, women.

1312
01:12:19,958 --> 01:12:21,333
Get off of me.

1313
01:12:22,666 --> 01:12:24,291
[panting]

1314
01:12:24,375 --> 01:12:26,833
If you touch her again, I'll kill you.

1315
01:12:26,916 --> 01:12:28,166
You understand?

1316
01:12:31,750 --> 01:12:33,708
Your money.

1317
01:12:38,166 --> 01:12:39,541
Shame.

1318
01:12:39,625 --> 01:12:41,416
She would have been fun.

1319
01:12:44,666 --> 01:12:46,083
Now get the fuck out of here!

1320
01:12:46,166 --> 01:12:48,708
You've got no reason
to come near us again.

1321
01:12:48,791 --> 01:12:49,875
Sure.

1322
01:12:49,958 --> 01:12:51,916
Until next time.

1323
01:12:52,000 --> 01:12:53,916
[laughs]

1324
01:12:55,458 --> 01:12:57,541
-You okay? You okay?
-I'm okay.

1325
01:12:57,625 --> 01:12:59,500
-You sure?
-I'm okay. I'm okay.

1326
01:12:59,583 --> 01:13:01,000
I'm okay.

1327
01:13:04,000 --> 01:13:05,333
Nice slap, by the way.

1328
01:13:05,416 --> 01:13:07,333
[both laughing]

1329
01:13:07,416 --> 01:13:10,041
Remind me to never make you mad.

1330
01:13:10,125 --> 01:13:11,333
[chuckles]

1331
01:13:16,041 --> 01:13:18,875
I'm really sorry about
not telling you about my mom.

1332
01:13:19,875 --> 01:13:21,791
I really thought I could fix it.

1333
01:13:21,875 --> 01:13:23,333
[quietly] It's okay.

1334
01:13:23,416 --> 01:13:25,083
It's not your fault.

1335
01:13:27,583 --> 01:13:29,583
[gentle music playing]

1336
01:13:38,000 --> 01:13:39,625
-[laughs]
-[chuckles]

1337
01:13:41,333 --> 01:13:42,375
Your dress.

1338
01:13:44,000 --> 01:13:45,208
It's ruined.

1339
01:13:46,791 --> 01:13:49,666
[chuckles] I was passing on
your ecological complaint.

1340
01:13:49,750 --> 01:13:50,958
[Julian chuckles]

1341
01:13:51,041 --> 01:13:53,333
That whole thing about the grass
and the chemicals.

1342
01:13:53,416 --> 01:13:54,625
-Wow.
-[laughs]

1343
01:14:03,541 --> 01:14:05,958
-[Julian] I need you now.
-[moans]

1344
01:14:09,875 --> 01:14:12,000
♪ ♪

1345
01:14:12,083 --> 01:14:14,000
[grunting]

1346
01:14:14,083 --> 01:14:16,375
[music tempo quickens]

1347
01:14:16,458 --> 01:14:17,375
[Ry exhales heavily]

1348
01:14:24,625 --> 01:14:25,791
[Julian chuckles]

1349
01:14:29,625 --> 01:14:31,625
[breathing heavily]

1350
01:14:37,250 --> 01:14:38,958
-[grunts]
-[sighs]

1351
01:14:42,916 --> 01:14:44,791
[breathing heavily]

1352
01:14:46,708 --> 01:14:48,041
[moaning]

1353
01:14:59,958 --> 01:15:01,875
[Isolde speaking indistinctly]

1354
01:15:01,958 --> 01:15:03,416
[lively chatter and music]

1355
01:15:08,291 --> 01:15:09,458
[speaking Spanish]

1356
01:15:11,958 --> 01:15:13,166
[Amara] Cheers.

1357
01:15:16,375 --> 01:15:17,541
-[phone vibrates]
-[scoffs softly]

1358
01:15:20,416 --> 01:15:23,708
[♪ Buscabulla sings "Tártaro"]

1359
01:15:23,791 --> 01:15:25,208
[Amara] Yeah.

1360
01:15:25,291 --> 01:15:28,500
It never ceases to amaze
what rich people will leave behind.

1361
01:15:28,583 --> 01:15:30,416
That lost and found is a treasure trove.

1362
01:15:30,500 --> 01:15:32,625
How do I look?

1363
01:15:32,708 --> 01:15:34,750
[laughs]

1364
01:15:37,791 --> 01:15:39,708
I'll see you guys down there.

1365
01:15:39,791 --> 01:15:41,416
[song continues with lyrics in Spanish]

1366
01:15:47,875 --> 01:15:49,875
♪ ♪

1367
01:15:55,916 --> 01:15:57,416
I'm just wondering if there's a way.

1368
01:15:57,500 --> 01:15:59,583
I agree, but I'm worried
that it's too late.

1369
01:15:59,666 --> 01:16:02,000
You ready?

1370
01:16:02,083 --> 01:16:03,500
Let's do it.

1371
01:16:04,500 --> 01:16:06,083
[Ry] Mom?

1372
01:16:06,166 --> 01:16:09,875
I want to introduce you to Julian Garcia.

1373
01:16:09,958 --> 01:16:12,625
It's a pleasure to meet you, <i>Señora Pera.</i>

1374
01:16:12,708 --> 01:16:14,458
I've heard a lot about you.

1375
01:16:16,375 --> 01:16:18,375
Let me get you both a drink.

1376
01:16:24,750 --> 01:16:28,250
Did you tell him who I am
and my association with Redwyn?

1377
01:16:28,333 --> 01:16:30,125
[softly] Yeah.

1378
01:16:31,583 --> 01:16:34,333
Did you tell him about your epilepsy?

1379
01:16:42,041 --> 01:16:43,750
<i>Gracias.</i>

1380
01:16:43,833 --> 01:16:46,333
[applause]

1381
01:16:46,416 --> 01:16:48,625
<i>Buenas noches. </i>Good evening.

1382
01:16:48,708 --> 01:16:52,125
Thank you all for-for being here with us
to celebrate

1383
01:16:52,208 --> 01:16:55,500
this exciting new chapter for Mallorca.

1384
01:16:55,583 --> 01:16:59,500
We are thrilled to introduce
an arts center that will

1385
01:16:59,583 --> 01:17:03,208
preserve the cultural heartbeat
of this beautiful island.

1386
01:17:03,291 --> 01:17:07,083
Now, some of you know I grew up here,
a long time ago,

1387
01:17:07,166 --> 01:17:10,791
so it's nice to have a chance
to be able to give back,

1388
01:17:10,875 --> 01:17:14,833
and not only with this amazing arts center

1389
01:17:14,916 --> 01:17:18,875
but by bringing
a world-class resort to Mallorca.

1390
01:17:18,958 --> 01:17:22,750
So let's raise a glass

1391
01:17:22,833 --> 01:17:24,375
and make a…

1392
01:17:27,666 --> 01:17:30,166
…and let's make a toast.

1393
01:17:30,250 --> 01:17:31,875
To Mallorca.

1394
01:17:31,958 --> 01:17:34,416
[crowd] To Mallorca.

1395
01:17:34,500 --> 01:17:36,416
[applause]

1396
01:17:36,500 --> 01:17:38,500
[lively chatter]

1397
01:17:40,208 --> 01:17:42,208
[band playing gentle guitar music]

1398
01:17:48,583 --> 01:17:49,708
Mateo.

1399
01:17:49,791 --> 01:17:51,125
<i>¿Cómo estás?</i>

1400
01:17:54,708 --> 01:17:56,708
It's really good to see you.

1401
01:17:58,583 --> 01:18:00,958
I never thought I would see you again.

1402
01:18:02,333 --> 01:18:03,750
It's been a long time.

1403
01:18:04,750 --> 01:18:06,166
Yes.

1404
01:18:08,791 --> 01:18:11,750
Um, look, I want to…

1405
01:18:11,833 --> 01:18:13,708
let you know that
none of this was personal.

1406
01:18:13,791 --> 01:18:15,958
Isolde…

1407
01:18:16,041 --> 01:18:18,791
everything between us is personal.

1408
01:18:19,875 --> 01:18:21,583
[chuckles softly]

1409
01:18:21,666 --> 01:18:24,791
I mean, I just want
to explain my intentions.

1410
01:18:24,875 --> 01:18:25,916
You don't need to explain anything.

1411
01:18:26,000 --> 01:18:28,250
I mean, you're right.

1412
01:18:28,333 --> 01:18:31,750
The island is changing,
and I can't keep it up anyways.

1413
01:18:31,833 --> 01:18:33,250
I tried.

1414
01:18:34,250 --> 01:18:36,958
I held on to my business
as long as I could.

1415
01:18:38,125 --> 01:18:39,916
But in the end…

1416
01:18:43,916 --> 01:18:46,666
-I just have one thing to ask of you.
-Yeah?

1417
01:18:46,750 --> 01:18:50,875
When you're building the hotel,
when you're shaping what comes next,

1418
01:18:50,958 --> 01:18:52,958
just don't forget about
what was here before.

1419
01:18:54,958 --> 01:18:57,375
I could never forget what was here before.

1420
01:18:58,666 --> 01:19:01,708
There is one good thing to come of this.

1421
01:19:03,041 --> 01:19:07,083
Maybe they will have the future
we never could.

1422
01:19:15,416 --> 01:19:17,041
Let's go.

1423
01:19:17,125 --> 01:19:19,458
This suit makes me feel like
I'm in a straitjacket.

1424
01:19:19,541 --> 01:19:20,708
[Ry chuckles]

1425
01:19:20,791 --> 01:19:22,666
[speaks Catalan]

1426
01:19:22,750 --> 01:19:24,291
Go be with your dad.

1427
01:19:24,375 --> 01:19:26,375
I'll find you later at the docks.

1428
01:19:27,833 --> 01:19:29,500
-See you later.
-Bye.

1429
01:19:30,500 --> 01:19:32,458
[gentle guitar music playing in distance]

1430
01:19:37,791 --> 01:19:42,166
I thought you said your stories about
growing up here would bore me.

1431
01:19:50,166 --> 01:19:51,875
[Isolde inhales deeply]

1432
01:19:51,958 --> 01:19:53,708
Mateo Garcia.

1433
01:19:53,791 --> 01:19:54,916
[Ry chuckles]

1434
01:19:55,000 --> 01:19:57,125
He was my first love.

1435
01:19:57,208 --> 01:20:01,791
We met when we were kids,
and as teenagers we couldn't…

1436
01:20:01,875 --> 01:20:03,875
stay away from each other.

1437
01:20:05,916 --> 01:20:10,291
He was the air I breathed
and the water I swam in.

1438
01:20:10,375 --> 01:20:12,125
[both chuckle]

1439
01:20:12,208 --> 01:20:15,666
We always talked about the future,
and we made plans and…

1440
01:20:19,000 --> 01:20:21,416
And then everything changed.

1441
01:20:22,458 --> 01:20:23,916
Your mom died.

1442
01:20:25,833 --> 01:20:29,333
I had never experienced a pain like that.

1443
01:20:32,166 --> 01:20:35,333
And every part of the island
just reminded me of her.

1444
01:20:38,583 --> 01:20:40,166
I had to leave. I had to escape.

1445
01:20:40,250 --> 01:20:42,875
Just wanted to get away. [sniffles]

1446
01:20:42,958 --> 01:20:44,458
I asked him to come with me.

1447
01:20:44,541 --> 01:20:46,250
I begged him.

1448
01:20:46,333 --> 01:20:47,458
[chuckles softly]

1449
01:20:48,833 --> 01:20:52,250
He didn't want to leave his family
or the business.

1450
01:20:54,625 --> 01:20:58,208
We wrote letters for years,
back and forth,

1451
01:20:58,291 --> 01:21:00,083
and then one day the letters stopped.

1452
01:21:06,791 --> 01:21:09,791
So when I found out
we were building this hotel

1453
01:21:09,875 --> 01:21:13,333
and buying the land,
I jumped at the chance to help him.

1454
01:21:15,666 --> 01:21:18,333
I wish you would have told me.

1455
01:21:18,416 --> 01:21:19,750
Yeah.

1456
01:21:19,833 --> 01:21:24,000
And now I'm just the face
that stole his family's dreams.

1457
01:21:24,083 --> 01:21:25,875
No. No.

1458
01:21:31,000 --> 01:21:34,000
-You did your best, Mom.
-[scoffs softly]

1459
01:21:34,083 --> 01:21:35,750
And he knows it.

1460
01:21:35,833 --> 01:21:37,000
Yeah.

1461
01:21:37,083 --> 01:21:39,791
[♪ Barzin sings "All the While"]

1462
01:21:42,291 --> 01:21:44,833
♪ <i>All summer</i> ♪

1463
01:21:44,916 --> 01:21:47,250
♪ <i>your love burned alone…</i>

1464
01:21:49,000 --> 01:21:51,375
Can we stay up tonight?

1465
01:21:51,458 --> 01:21:52,625
Mm-hmm.

1466
01:21:53,875 --> 01:21:55,500
I've never seen a sunrise.

1467
01:21:56,916 --> 01:21:59,125
-What do you mean?
-[chuckles]

1468
01:21:59,208 --> 01:22:00,333
From the water?

1469
01:22:01,583 --> 01:22:02,875
[whispers] From anywhere.

1470
01:22:05,375 --> 01:22:06,791
Well…

1471
01:22:08,375 --> 01:22:11,041
…I can get you
the best seat in the house.

1472
01:22:11,125 --> 01:22:13,833
-Hmm?
-Mm-hmm.

1473
01:22:13,916 --> 01:22:17,375
♪ <i>Beside the girl</i> ♪

1474
01:22:19,708 --> 01:22:22,583
♪ <i>Did you wait for</i> ♪

1475
01:22:22,666 --> 01:22:25,416
♪ <i>something to change you?</i> ♪

1476
01:22:28,500 --> 01:22:31,708
♪ <i>All the while you wait</i> ♪

1477
01:22:31,791 --> 01:22:33,583
♪ <i>for your heart</i> ♪

1478
01:22:36,833 --> 01:22:40,000
♪ <i>All the while you wait</i> ♪

1479
01:22:40,083 --> 01:22:43,291
♪ <i>for your heart to…</i> ♪

1480
01:22:43,375 --> 01:22:44,500
Look.

1481
01:22:44,583 --> 01:22:46,208
♪ <i>Wake up…</i>

1482
01:22:47,541 --> 01:22:48,583
[gasps]

1483
01:22:48,666 --> 01:22:51,333
-♪ <i>For your heart</i> ♪
-[chuckles]

1484
01:22:51,416 --> 01:22:54,541
♪ <i>to wake up</i> ♪♪

1485
01:22:56,000 --> 01:22:59,375
Thank you for saving
your first sunrise for me.

1486
01:23:01,666 --> 01:23:04,708
You can have all my firsts
and all my lasts.

1487
01:23:04,791 --> 01:23:06,750
♪ ♪

1488
01:23:17,416 --> 01:23:18,791
[chuckles]

1489
01:23:21,250 --> 01:23:22,458
[sighs]

1490
01:23:28,958 --> 01:23:30,458
[exhales softly]

1491
01:23:30,541 --> 01:23:32,791
[song fades]

1492
01:23:38,041 --> 01:23:39,750
Mom, is everything okay?

1493
01:23:40,916 --> 01:23:43,166
When did you stop taking your meds?

1494
01:23:50,583 --> 01:23:53,041
A few days after we arrived.

1495
01:23:56,666 --> 01:23:58,291
They made me feel numb.

1496
01:23:58,375 --> 01:24:00,750
Mom, I needed a single summer
of feeling something.

1497
01:24:00,833 --> 01:24:01,833
I'm such an idiot.

1498
01:24:01,916 --> 01:24:03,291
I should have never left you alone.

1499
01:24:03,375 --> 01:24:05,000
-Stop. No.
-I should've stayed on top of you…

1500
01:24:05,083 --> 01:24:06,666
-It's my decision!
-…to make sure you took your pills!

1501
01:24:06,750 --> 01:24:08,458
No. It's my decision.

1502
01:24:08,541 --> 01:24:10,625
You probably made everything worse!

1503
01:24:10,708 --> 01:24:13,416
[voice breaking] I don't care.
I don't care.

1504
01:24:13,500 --> 01:24:14,666
-I care.
-I don't.

1505
01:24:14,750 --> 01:24:16,083
Okay.

1506
01:24:16,166 --> 01:24:18,333
-What are you doing?
-Let's go. We're leaving.

1507
01:24:18,416 --> 01:24:19,583
No, no, we're not.

1508
01:24:19,666 --> 01:24:22,000
-We're leaving.
-No. No, please.

1509
01:24:22,083 --> 01:24:23,750
Mom, I saw the sun rise
for the first time.

1510
01:24:23,833 --> 01:24:25,375
You did? That's great.

1511
01:24:25,458 --> 01:24:27,166
I can feel things.
I can feel Julian touching me,

1512
01:24:27,250 --> 01:24:30,291
and I could feel the sea on my skin.

1513
01:24:30,375 --> 01:24:33,666
[laughs] At least there's something
worth remembering.

1514
01:24:35,750 --> 01:24:38,250
[sobs] I want to stay here.

1515
01:24:40,291 --> 01:24:42,458
I want to live.

1516
01:24:43,500 --> 01:24:45,666
You want to stay here?

1517
01:24:45,750 --> 01:24:48,041
Oh, you want to live.
Now you want to live.

1518
01:24:48,125 --> 01:24:51,041
For how long, Ry?
How long do you want to live?

1519
01:24:52,083 --> 01:24:53,500
We're leaving.

1520
01:24:53,583 --> 01:24:55,250
I told Lena to move up our flight.

1521
01:24:56,583 --> 01:24:57,708
No.

1522
01:24:57,791 --> 01:24:59,125
Pack your stuff, Ry. Let's go.

1523
01:24:59,208 --> 01:25:01,041
No, Mom.

1524
01:25:01,125 --> 01:25:02,250
No.

1525
01:25:02,333 --> 01:25:03,666
Ry!

1526
01:25:04,708 --> 01:25:06,416
-[panting]
-[tense music playing]

1527
01:25:07,458 --> 01:25:08,916
-[muffled] Ry!
-[heart beating rapidly]

1528
01:25:09,000 --> 01:25:10,125
Ry?

1529
01:25:10,208 --> 01:25:11,541
[audio continues distorted]

1530
01:25:11,625 --> 01:25:13,625
Ry, where are you going?

1531
01:25:15,125 --> 01:25:16,333
[gasping]

1532
01:25:16,416 --> 01:25:18,916
Ry? Ry!

1533
01:25:19,000 --> 01:25:21,708
[heart beating faster]

1534
01:25:21,791 --> 01:25:24,625
[whimpering]

1535
01:25:24,708 --> 01:25:27,875
-[grunting]
-[ears ringing]

1536
01:25:32,666 --> 01:25:34,500
Ry!

1537
01:25:37,791 --> 01:25:39,750
♪ ♪

1538
01:26:02,000 --> 01:26:03,875
-[Isolde] <i>Move, move, move! Ry!</i>
-[water rushing]

1539
01:26:03,958 --> 01:26:05,041
[audio continues clearly]

1540
01:26:05,125 --> 01:26:06,208
Hey, hey, hey. Shh.

1541
01:26:06,291 --> 01:26:08,708
It's okay. You're okay, baby. You're okay.

1542
01:26:08,791 --> 01:26:11,000
I'm right here. I'm right here.

1543
01:26:11,083 --> 01:26:12,958
Everything's gonna be okay.

1544
01:26:13,041 --> 01:26:14,750
[heart monitor beeping steadily]

1545
01:26:14,833 --> 01:26:15,958
[whispers] I'm here.

1546
01:26:16,041 --> 01:26:17,833
[chuckles] There you are.

1547
01:26:18,875 --> 01:26:20,833
[crickets chirping]

1548
01:26:20,916 --> 01:26:23,291
-[breathlessly] Hi.
-[Isolde] Hey. Perfect timing.

1549
01:26:23,375 --> 01:26:24,916
-[door closes]
-I'm gonna go get a coffee.

1550
01:26:25,000 --> 01:26:26,416
Okay.

1551
01:26:26,500 --> 01:26:28,208
I'll be right back.

1552
01:26:30,083 --> 01:26:31,458
[door opens]

1553
01:26:31,541 --> 01:26:34,166
Oh. There she is.

1554
01:26:34,250 --> 01:26:37,083
Girl, I was high-key worried.

1555
01:26:37,166 --> 01:26:39,125
I would've come earlier,
but my boss made me

1556
01:26:39,208 --> 01:26:40,916
do, like, actual work.

1557
01:26:41,958 --> 01:26:44,666
You kept all this on the DL.

1558
01:26:44,750 --> 01:26:45,958
Ah?

1559
01:26:46,041 --> 01:26:48,583
Epilepsy and tubers?

1560
01:26:48,666 --> 01:26:50,791
Not to be confused with tumors,

1561
01:26:50,875 --> 01:26:53,166
although they sound just as shit.

1562
01:26:55,208 --> 01:26:56,916
I'm sorry for the secrets.

1563
01:26:57,000 --> 01:26:59,041
I get it.

1564
01:26:59,125 --> 01:27:00,958
You were looking for fun.

1565
01:27:01,041 --> 01:27:03,541
Which is why you gravitated to me. Hmm?

1566
01:27:06,541 --> 01:27:08,250
Speaking of fun, where's Prisha?

1567
01:27:08,333 --> 01:27:09,375
Is she here?

1568
01:27:09,458 --> 01:27:11,208
No.

1569
01:27:11,291 --> 01:27:14,291
All good things must come to an end.

1570
01:27:14,375 --> 01:27:15,458
She went home?

1571
01:27:15,541 --> 01:27:17,750
Yeah. But would I do it again?

1572
01:27:21,000 --> 01:27:22,250
Hell yeah, baby.

1573
01:27:24,291 --> 01:27:27,000
-[ticking]
-[monitor beeping steadily]

1574
01:27:52,166 --> 01:27:54,166
[gentle music playing]

1575
01:28:04,083 --> 01:28:05,666
[Julian] What happened?

1576
01:28:14,583 --> 01:28:15,791
Are you hurt?

1577
01:28:17,958 --> 01:28:20,125
I have tuberous sclerosis.

1578
01:28:22,041 --> 01:28:23,375
Causes epilepsy.

1579
01:28:24,666 --> 01:28:26,333
I was born with it.

1580
01:28:32,125 --> 01:28:34,333
What-what can we do?
Is there, is there a treatment?

1581
01:28:34,416 --> 01:28:36,875
Yes and no.

1582
01:28:36,958 --> 01:28:39,333
Medication helps,
but it's never been consistent.

1583
01:28:40,916 --> 01:28:43,416
And when I got here,
I stopped taking it altogether.

1584
01:28:43,500 --> 01:28:44,833
Why?

1585
01:28:46,416 --> 01:28:48,583
[voice breaking] Because it made me
feel numb.

1586
01:28:50,083 --> 01:28:52,833
Julian, I don't want to feel numb anymore.

1587
01:28:59,958 --> 01:29:01,625
Is surgery an option?

1588
01:29:01,708 --> 01:29:05,083
Yes, but there's too much risk.

1589
01:29:05,166 --> 01:29:06,875
I could lose my memory.

1590
01:29:14,250 --> 01:29:16,000
So…

1591
01:29:16,083 --> 01:29:18,500
so would that be the worst thing?

1592
01:29:18,583 --> 01:29:19,750
You would be healthy.

1593
01:29:21,166 --> 01:29:23,500
Everything I know would be gone.

1594
01:29:29,916 --> 01:29:32,125
Why didn't you tell me any of this?

1595
01:29:35,416 --> 01:29:38,291
Because I wanted to figure it out…

1596
01:29:39,458 --> 01:29:41,500
…for myself…

1597
01:29:43,041 --> 01:29:44,583
…what I'm living for.

1598
01:29:47,083 --> 01:29:49,000
And it's this place.

1599
01:29:52,208 --> 01:29:53,625
It's…

1600
01:29:55,291 --> 01:29:58,708
It's watching my mom do what she loves.

1601
01:29:59,750 --> 01:30:03,250
It's watching Amara
try a new makeup trend.

1602
01:30:05,708 --> 01:30:08,625
It's sitting in a dark cave with you…

1603
01:30:10,000 --> 01:30:13,458
…because you make darkness
feel peaceful.

1604
01:30:16,125 --> 01:30:18,083
Losing those memories…

1605
01:30:20,125 --> 01:30:22,708
…or the ability to make new ones…

1606
01:30:27,125 --> 01:30:29,125
…that's worse than death.

1607
01:30:33,708 --> 01:30:35,666
♪ ♪

1608
01:30:39,958 --> 01:30:42,458
[Julian breathes deeply]

1609
01:30:42,541 --> 01:30:44,291
I love you, Oriah.

1610
01:30:44,375 --> 01:30:45,583
[Ry chuckles]

1611
01:30:50,458 --> 01:30:52,375
[voice breaking] I love you, too.

1612
01:30:52,458 --> 01:30:54,458
♪ ♪

1613
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:13,083
[sighs]

1614
01:31:16,958 --> 01:31:18,000
[sighs]

1615
01:31:19,375 --> 01:31:20,458
Ry?

1616
01:31:35,541 --> 01:31:36,750
[whispers] Ry.

1617
01:31:39,833 --> 01:31:41,625
Ry.

1618
01:31:44,916 --> 01:31:46,166
Ry.

1619
01:31:50,625 --> 01:31:51,833
Ry.

1620
01:31:53,291 --> 01:31:54,625
Ry!

1621
01:31:54,708 --> 01:31:56,208
No, no. Oriah!

1622
01:31:56,291 --> 01:31:57,500
Ry!

1623
01:32:01,708 --> 01:32:03,458
<i>Papá. Papá. Papá.</i>

1624
01:32:03,541 --> 01:32:05,541
[speaking urgently]

1625
01:32:08,958 --> 01:32:10,083
Ry, please.

1626
01:32:10,166 --> 01:32:12,166
[pensive music playing]

1627
01:32:16,166 --> 01:32:17,375
[EMT] Faint pulse.

1628
01:32:17,458 --> 01:32:18,791
She stopped breathing at the scene

1629
01:32:18,875 --> 01:32:20,791
-but stabilized in transport.
-Stay with me, okay?

1630
01:32:20,875 --> 01:32:22,708
I'm gonna be here, okay?

1631
01:32:22,791 --> 01:32:24,833
[doctor] <i>She's holding on, but barely.</i>

1632
01:32:24,916 --> 01:32:27,625
Scans show her condition has progressed.

1633
01:32:27,708 --> 01:32:31,125
It's your decision,
but we would strongly recommend surgery.

1634
01:32:34,375 --> 01:32:35,958
I mean, what is there to think about?

1635
01:32:36,041 --> 01:32:38,000
Ry has never wanted surgery.

1636
01:32:38,083 --> 01:32:41,708
I've tried to convince her for years,
and she made me promise.

1637
01:32:41,791 --> 01:32:45,625
We can stabilize her,
keep her comfortable.

1638
01:32:45,708 --> 01:32:48,333
But without surgery,
her condition will deteriorate,

1639
01:32:48,416 --> 01:32:51,000
and it will just be a matter of time.

1640
01:32:51,083 --> 01:32:53,083
Isolde…

1641
01:32:54,750 --> 01:32:57,166
…I understand the risks,

1642
01:32:57,250 --> 01:33:00,083
and Oriah spoke to me about her wishes.

1643
01:33:01,333 --> 01:33:05,541
But while there is a chance
that we could save her

1644
01:33:05,625 --> 01:33:08,125
and a chance she could have
a normal life…

1645
01:33:10,041 --> 01:33:12,875
…I beg you to take it.

1646
01:33:14,666 --> 01:33:18,791
She was worried about losing
the best parts of her life.

1647
01:33:19,833 --> 01:33:22,125
But if this works,

1648
01:33:22,208 --> 01:33:25,458
her favorite memories will be
the ones ahead of her.

1649
01:33:25,541 --> 01:33:27,500
♪ ♪

1650
01:33:41,416 --> 01:33:43,375
[heart monitor beeping steadily]

1651
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:46,958
[pensive music playing]

1652
01:34:05,541 --> 01:34:07,541
[heart monitor beeping steadily]

1653
01:34:14,666 --> 01:34:17,500
[Isolde] She has the same condition
my mother had.

1654
01:34:18,541 --> 01:34:20,208
I'm so sorry, Izzy.

1655
01:34:24,875 --> 01:34:26,791
Does she know?

1656
01:34:28,250 --> 01:34:30,458
That I gave her this…

1657
01:34:30,541 --> 01:34:32,000
horrible thing that's hurting her?

1658
01:34:32,083 --> 01:34:33,500
No, she doesn't.

1659
01:34:34,750 --> 01:34:36,416
She wouldn't blame you.

1660
01:34:38,625 --> 01:34:41,041
You know, I never planned to have a baby.

1661
01:34:42,583 --> 01:34:43,750
Wasn't on my list.

1662
01:34:43,833 --> 01:34:46,166
No.

1663
01:34:46,250 --> 01:34:50,750
If I remember correctly, you wanted
a mansion, three cars and a pony.

1664
01:34:52,625 --> 01:34:53,833
I never got the pony.

1665
01:34:55,041 --> 01:34:58,083
When I found out I was pregnant, I…

1666
01:34:58,166 --> 01:35:00,333
I felt like my life had purpose.

1667
01:35:02,208 --> 01:35:04,208
And I wanted her so bad.

1668
01:35:05,750 --> 01:35:08,375
And I thought I would just
take the chance.

1669
01:35:08,458 --> 01:35:11,666
And you have raised a strong young woman

1670
01:35:11,750 --> 01:35:13,916
and gave her a wonderful life.

1671
01:35:16,291 --> 01:35:20,125
So whatever happens, Izzy,
you have nothing to be ashamed of.

1672
01:35:21,833 --> 01:35:23,583
Hmm? Nothing.

1673
01:35:27,625 --> 01:35:29,583
[contemplative music playing]

1674
01:35:56,958 --> 01:35:58,916
♪ ♪

1675
01:36:02,125 --> 01:36:03,833
Hey, thanks for coming.

1676
01:36:03,916 --> 01:36:07,000
-No, of course.
-We have a lot of work to do.

1677
01:36:07,083 --> 01:36:08,875
Yeah, so we have a couple of solutions,

1678
01:36:08,958 --> 01:36:10,375
but they're pretty complex.

1679
01:36:12,125 --> 01:36:14,125
[conversing in Catalan]

1680
01:36:14,708 --> 01:36:15,833
I'll take that one.

1681
01:36:16,875 --> 01:36:18,875
♪ ♪

1682
01:36:29,208 --> 01:36:31,708
That is excellent news. Thank you.

1683
01:36:38,458 --> 01:36:40,458
-Julian.
-Isolde.

1684
01:36:40,541 --> 01:36:42,625
Hey. Sit down. Sit down.

1685
01:36:45,625 --> 01:36:47,041
I…

1686
01:36:49,791 --> 01:36:52,541
I have something that belongs to you.

1687
01:36:54,708 --> 01:36:56,500
♪ ♪

1688
01:36:58,791 --> 01:37:00,916
When I was eight,

1689
01:37:01,000 --> 01:37:04,250
I found my father's letters
to his first love.

1690
01:37:05,625 --> 01:37:08,250
I always wondered who they were for.

1691
01:37:10,125 --> 01:37:13,250
And now I know who Izzy is.

1692
01:37:16,958 --> 01:37:18,166
[sighs]

1693
01:37:20,208 --> 01:37:21,750
[inhales]

1694
01:37:21,833 --> 01:37:23,208
[Isolde sighs]

1695
01:37:24,208 --> 01:37:25,291
[Mateo] Hey, guys.

1696
01:37:27,166 --> 01:37:28,291
Hey.

1697
01:37:28,375 --> 01:37:30,875
-You speak to the doctor?
-Uh, no.

1698
01:37:30,958 --> 01:37:33,416
No, I-I, um…

1699
01:37:33,500 --> 01:37:36,375
I haven't. There's been no-no change
with that, but…

1700
01:37:38,000 --> 01:37:41,416
…there has been a… a new development.

1701
01:37:48,375 --> 01:37:52,041
So you found a new plot of land
to build the hotel?

1702
01:37:54,916 --> 01:37:57,208
I know how much your business
means to you.

1703
01:37:57,291 --> 01:37:59,875
And I thought it was too late, but it's…

1704
01:37:59,958 --> 01:38:01,708
it's never too late.

1705
01:38:04,125 --> 01:38:05,291
You were right.

1706
01:38:05,375 --> 01:38:07,166
This is my home.

1707
01:38:08,166 --> 01:38:10,208
And I should be protecting it.

1708
01:38:10,291 --> 01:38:12,250
So…

1709
01:38:12,333 --> 01:38:15,000
we are investing in your business.

1710
01:38:15,083 --> 01:38:16,500
[chuckles softly]

1711
01:38:16,583 --> 01:38:18,583
It's what Ry would want.

1712
01:38:19,708 --> 01:38:21,666
It's what I want.

1713
01:38:23,208 --> 01:38:25,125
I think…

1714
01:38:25,208 --> 01:38:27,125
we will need to get you
one of these shirts, too.

1715
01:38:27,208 --> 01:38:28,375
[both chuckle]

1716
01:38:31,958 --> 01:38:34,250
Thank you, Izzy.

1717
01:38:34,333 --> 01:38:36,291
Can't wait to work together.

1718
01:38:38,291 --> 01:38:40,875
♪ ♪

1719
01:38:46,250 --> 01:38:47,708
[in Catalan]
I like the boat.

1720
01:38:47,958 --> 01:38:49,958
-It's good.
-[phone vibrating]

1721
01:38:50,208 --> 01:38:51,375
One second.

1722
01:38:53,458 --> 01:38:54,458
Yes.

1723
01:38:55,791 --> 01:38:57,000
[in English] Ry's awake.

1724
01:38:57,083 --> 01:38:58,041
[in Catalan] She's awake!

1725
01:39:02,000 --> 01:39:03,666
Welcome back, sweetie.

1726
01:39:03,750 --> 01:39:05,208
[panting]

1727
01:39:05,291 --> 01:39:06,500
Ry.

1728
01:39:13,166 --> 01:39:17,500
[Ry] <i>My memories come back to me</i>
<i>one by one.</i>

1729
01:39:20,750 --> 01:39:24,208
<i>I feel like I could touch him,</i>

1730
01:39:24,291 --> 01:39:26,375
<i>someone I used to know.</i>

1731
01:39:30,500 --> 01:39:32,166
<i>I wonder…</i>

1732
01:39:34,500 --> 01:39:36,916
<i>…will fate keep following me here?</i>

1733
01:39:42,000 --> 01:39:45,250
<i>What I once thought would be</i>
<i>my last summer,</i>

1734
01:39:45,333 --> 01:39:48,416
<i>my first and last sunrise…</i>

1735
01:39:48,500 --> 01:39:51,166
[♪ sombr sings
"do i ever cross your mind"]

1736
01:39:51,250 --> 01:39:54,458
<i>…ended up being the beginning</i>
<i>of my life.</i>

1737
01:40:01,291 --> 01:40:02,708
[Julian] <i>Hola.</i>

1738
01:40:02,791 --> 01:40:04,083
I'm Julian.

1739
01:40:04,166 --> 01:40:06,875
♪ <i>When you lay awake at night</i> ♪

1740
01:40:06,958 --> 01:40:09,708
♪ <i>do I ever cross your mind?</i> ♪

1741
01:40:09,791 --> 01:40:12,625
♪ <i>'Cause you still cross mine</i> ♪

1742
